; Process identities are local to one host, PID namespace and boot.
; Started is /proc/<pid>/stat field 22: clock ticks since boot, not wall time.
; A persisted binding must be invalidated when its observed boot changes;
; Pid and Started alone cannot detect a different boot.

Library ; Shared process data, observation capability and its bearer.
[] ; Imports: the contract uses intrinsic types only.
[ ; Types: a process identity, its ordered ancestry and observation refusals.
   Pid.Integer
   Started.Integer
   Process.{ Pid Started } ; A process identifier and its kernel start ticks.
   Ancestry.Vector<Process> ; Sending CLI first, its parents next, namespace init last.
   Unidentified.[ ; Why a claimed process chain cannot be trusted.
      PeerMismatch
      Vanished
      Reused
      Malformed ] ]
[ ; Traits: observation of an existing process identity.
   Identifiable.[ ; Re-observe this process and its complete parent chain.
      identify.[ Result<Ancestry Unidentified> ] ] ] ; Yield the witnessed chain or a refusal.
[ ; Associations: Process bears the observation capability.
   Process.[ Identifiable ] ] ; The implementation belongs to Process.

; identify re-observes this Process and its parent chain from the kernel.
; It refuses a vanished process, changed start ticks, or malformed chain.
; The receiver anchors the first claimed element to socket peer credentials,
; re-observes that peer and its ancestry, and compares the entire chain.
; A nonempty, ordered claim is required; a live unrelated process is no proof.
; Shells and wrappers remain in the witnessed chain; none are skipped here.
; Flow alone searches that validated ancestry for an address binding.
